      "id": "2052853466637476317",
      "text": "RT @Dr_TheHistories: The Iliad and Odyssey are the only nearly complete survivors of the Epic Cycle, an 8 part collection of ancient Greek…",
      "created_at": "Fri May 08 20:49:41 +0000 2026",
      "lang": "en",
      "media": [],
      "retweet": {
        "id": "2052614168659050987",
        "text": "The Iliad and Odyssey are the only nearly complete survivors of the Epic Cycle, an 8 part collection of ancient Greek epics that once told the full mythological story of the Trojan War.\n\nHomer’s poems cover only a small portion of this larger saga, with the Iliad focusing on a brief period near the end of the war and the Odyssey detailing Odysseus’ return home. \n\nThe other lost epics, including the Cypria, Aethiopis, Little Iliad, Iliou Persis, Nostoi, and Telegony, expanded the narrative to include the origins of the war, Achilles’ later battles, the fall of Troy, the Greek heroes’ returns, and Odysseus’ final fate. \n\nThough these poems were once foundational to Greek literary culture, they were gradually lost as manuscript traditions declined, leaving behind only fragments, summaries, and references from later classical writers.\n\n#drthehistories",
        "created_at": "Fri May 08 04:58:48 +0000 2026",
        "lang": "en",
        "media": [
